## Bijection Learning algorithm ports and prompt text

Source: https://github.com/haizelabs/bijection-learning, specifically
`that_good_infra/transformations.py` (bijection construction, encoding,
decoding) and `run_bijection_attacks.py` (prompt construction).
Paper: Brian R. Y. Huang, Maximilian Li, Leonard Tang, "Endless Jailbreaks with
Bijection Learning," arXiv:2410.01294 (ICLR 2025, Haize Labs).

The following are ported from the upstream repo and ship inside this wheel:

- `src/bijection_optimizer/bijection.py`: verbatim ports of
  `BijectionLanguage.create_bijective_mapping`,
  `DigitBijectionLanguage.create_bijective_mapping_digits`, `permute_string`
  (both encode and decode directions), `DigitBijectionLanguage._f`, and
  `permute_digits_to_string` — including upstream's leading-delimiter behaviour
  in digit decoding, which is retained deliberately and pinned by tests.
- `src/bijection_optimizer/prompts.py`: the teaching-intro template (the
  "Language Alpha" preamble and alphabet table) from the letter / digit branches
  of `full_attack_construction`, and `MULTITURN_INDICATOR` from
  `run_bijection_attacks.py`.
- The run-script defaults `max_attempts = 6` and `num_teaching_shots = 10`, and
  the paper's main-table digit configuration (`num_digits = 2`,
  `digit_delimiter = "  "`, `fixed_size = 10`).

